Where to get the source code of BetterGuac and what it ships
=============================================================

BetterGuac itself
  https://github.com/BondJamesB07/BetterGuac
  Every release is tagged (v1.6.0-bg10 for this release). The tag holds the
  BetterGuac code, the patches applied to Apache Guacamole and the build
  scripts that produce the .deb and Docker image.

Apache Guacamole 1.6.0 (Apache License 2.0)
  https://guacamole.apache.org/releases/1.6.0/
  https://archive.apache.org/dist/guacamole/1.6.0/source/
  guacamole-server-1.6.0.tar.gz (guacd), guacamole-client-1.6.0.tar.gz (the
  web application), guacamole-auth-jdbc-1.6.0.tar.gz and
  guacamole-auth-totp-1.6.0.tar.gz. BetterGuac's changes are in patches/ in
  the BetterGuac source and listed in NOTICE.

Third-party Java libraries inside the web application
  The Apache Guacamole web application (guacamole.war) bundles libraries
  under their own licenses. Their licenses are in META-INF/LICENSE and
  META-INF/bundled/ inside the WAR. These are shipped unmodified, as they
  come in the Apache Guacamole 1.6.0 release. The ones under the Eclipse
  Public License 2.0 or the CDDL 1.1, and where their source is:
    Eclipse Jersey 2.46 ........ https://github.com/eclipse-ee4j/jersey (tag 2.46)
    Eclipse HK2 2.6.1 .......... https://github.com/eclipse-ee4j/glassfish-hk2 (tag 2.6.1)
    Jakarta Annotations 1.3.5 .. https://github.com/jakartaee/common-annotations-api (tag 1.3.5)
    Jakarta Activation 1.2.2 ... https://github.com/jakartaee/jaf-api (tag 1.2.2)
    Jakarta RESTful WS 2.1.6 ... https://github.com/jakartaee/rest (tag 2.1.6)
    Jakarta Inject (HK2) 2.6.1 . https://github.com/eclipse-ee4j/glassfish-hk2 (tag 2.6.1)
    OSGi Resource Locator 1.0.3  https://github.com/eclipse-ee4j/glassfish-hk2-extra (tag 1.0.3-RELEASE)
    JSR-250 API 1.0 ............ https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/javax/annotation/jsr250-api/1.0/
    Logback 1.3.15 (EPL 1.0 /
      LGPL 2.1) ................ https://github.com/qos-ch/logback (tag v_1.3.15)
  Source jars for all of them are also on Maven Central,
  https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/, next to each library's binary jar.

  For Tomcat 10, betterguac-setup converts the WAR and the extensions from
  javax.* to jakarta.* on the machine where BetterGuac is installed, with
  Debian's Apache Tomcat migration tool (package tomcat-jakartaee-migration,
  Apache License 2.0). The converted copy lives in /var/cache/betterguac and
  is rebuilt by: sudo betterguac-admin webapp

Debian and Ubuntu packages (Docker image)
  The Docker image is built on debian:trixie-slim and contains Debian
  packages under their own licenses, some under the GNU GPL (for example
  mariadb-server, GPL-2, and libvncclient1, GPL-2+). The image lists every
  package with its exact version in /usr/share/betterguac/legal/sbom/:
    packages.tsv           package, version, architecture, source package
    betterguac.spdx.json   the same as an SPDX 2.3 document
  Each package's license is in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright in the
  image. The corresponding source code of each package and version is
  available from the Debian archive:
    https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/ (and https://snapshot.debian.org/
    for exact past versions), or with: apt-get source <package>=<version>
  Questions about the source: https://github.com/BondJamesB07/BetterGuac/issues
